INTERPRETATION
For each even level k, even label q with 2q<k, and 2<=s<=20, the exact
finite-fusion scan tests every coordinate of

f_(2s)(N_q^(2s+1))_(0,x)-f_(2s+1)(N_q^(2s))_(0,x).

No negative value occurs through level 300.  If this hierarchy were proved
for arbitrary s,k,q, the semigroup identity would give D_(j,s)>=0 whenever
2s+1<=2j+2-2s, removing the lower half of every cumulative prefix.
This is bounded discovery, not that proof.

The complementary upper-half proposal

g_(2p)(N_q^(2p))_(0,x)-g_(2p-1)(N_q^(2p+1))_(0,x)>=0

is false for every tested p.  Therefore the lower hierarchy cannot be
mirrored to prove the remaining upper slices determinant by determinant.

